<title>BELGIUM: SGB sees full-year 1996 net rising.</title>
<headline>SGB sees full-year 1996 net rising.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale de Belgique (SGB), Belgium's flagship holding company, said on Tuesday it expected full-year 1996 current profit to match 1995's, but net profit to rise.</p>
<p>&quot;In the present economic and monetary climate group net income on ordinary activities in 1996 should be at least up to the 1995 level. Its net profit, on the other hand, will be higher,&quot; SGB said in a statement on first-half earnings.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
